{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS26WRW7uWqD7kE5QZgf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WjMLKipwFc4bea3oFtpwmu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -i 's/\"value\": lo, \"end\": hi/\"start\": lo, \"end\": hi/' gen.py && sed -i 's|\"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete.s LTHR.\"\"\"|\"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete'\"'\"'s LTHR.\\n\\n    The lower bound must be called \"start\", not \"value\": \"value\" is exported\\n    to FIT as a Lap-HR/zone target (the watch clamps it to its own zones),\\n    \"start\"+\"end\" becomes an Instant-HR corridor in raw bpm.\\n    \"\"\"|' gen.py && python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json | head -12\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'EOF'\n# Fix: HR corridors clamped to the watch's own zones\n\n## Change\n`gen.py`, `hr_target()`: the lower bound key is now `start` instead of `value`:\n`{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`.\n\n## Why\n`readback/watch-notes.md` shows every corridor displayed as a watch zone band\n(e.g. planned 75–82% = 129–141 bpm, shown 137–151), even though the API\naccepted and returned the event unchanged. `{value, end}` is exported to FIT\nas a Lap-HR / zone target, which the watch clamps to its own zones (LTHR 168).\n`{start, end}` is exported as an Instant-HR corridor in raw bpm computed by\nIntervals from its stored LTHR (172). Units stay `%lthr`, so Intervals does the\nconversion (the absolute-bpm attempts gave 214–249 and 101).\n\n## Which parts of the colleague's note I used\n- Used: the `start`/`end` vs `value`/`end` finding, and keeping `%lthr` units\n  (matches our earlier failed bpm attempts in the watch notes).\n- Not used: the top-level `description` text grammar. Our readback has\n  `workout_doc.steps` populated and the problem reported is the watch targets,\n  not the web UI. Adding it would be unverified here and, per the note, a\n  parser stumble erases both representations. Worth doing separately if the\n  web UI shows no step chart.\n- Not used: the reproduction steps (they need the API key, athlete id and a\n  watch sync).\n\n## Not verified\nI could not push or sync a watch (no credentials, nothing external sent). To\nverify: push `gen.py` output, read it back (`steps` must be non-empty), sync,\nand expect Tempo 151–160, Float 129–141 on the watch.\nEOF\ngit diff --stat"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1647,"cache_read_input_tokens":22890,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1647},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d355349-48f0-4681-b137-31f1bf4ad68d","uuid":"e2580458-2ce6-4a5d-8dcf-5e7896548e44","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:19:14.120Z","request_id":"req_011CgS26WAP7N6vvBteyJSii","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WjMLKipwFc4bea3oFtpwmu":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-2j7F2e && sed -i 's/\"value\": lo, \"end\": hi/\"start\": lo, \"end\": hi/' gen.py && sed -i 's|\"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete.s LTHR.\"\"\"|\"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete'\"'\"'s LTHR.\\n\\n    The lower bound must be called \"start\", not \"value\": \"value\" is exported\\n    to FIT as a Lap-HR/zone target (the watch clamps it to its own zones),\\n    \"start\"+\"end\" becomes an Instant-HR corridor in raw bpm.\\n    \"\"\"|' gen.py && python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json | head -12\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'EOF'\n# Fix: HR corridors clamped to the watch's own zones\n\n## Change\n`gen.py`, `hr_target()`: the lower bound key is now `start` instead of `value`:\n`{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`.\n\n## Why\n`readback/watch-notes.md` shows every corridor displayed as a watch zone band\n(e.g. planned 75–82% = 129–141 bpm, shown 137–151), even though the API\naccepted and returned the event unchanged. `{value, end}` is exported to FIT\nas a Lap-HR / zone target, which the watch clamps to its own zones (LTHR 168).\n`{start, end}` is exported as an Instant-HR corridor in raw bpm computed by\nIntervals from its stored LTHR (172). Units stay `%lthr`, so Intervals does the\nconversion (the absolute-bpm attempts gave 214–249 and 101).\n\n## Which parts of the colleague's note I used\n- Used: the `start`/`end` vs `value`/`end` finding, and keeping `%lthr` units\n  (matches our earlier failed bpm attempts in the watch notes).\n- Not used: the top-level `description` text grammar. Our readback has\n  `workout_doc.steps` populated and the problem reported is the watch targets,\n  not the web UI. Adding it would be unverified here and, per the note, a\n  parser stumble erases both representations. Worth doing separately if the\n  web UI shows no step chart.\n- Not used: the reproduction steps (they need the API key, athlete id and a\n  watch sync).\n\n## Not verified\nI could not push or sync a watch (no credentials, nothing external sent). To\nverify: push `gen.py` output, read it back (`steps` must be non-empty), sync,\nand expect Tempo 151–160, Float 129–141 on the watch.\nEOF\ngit diff --stat"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01WjMLKipwFc4bea3oFtpwmu":{"cwd":"/private/tmp/h-2j7F2e"}}}
